    "created_at": "2025-04-11T10:19:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-11T10:19:02Z",
    "body": "Feels a bit overkill. I'd assume the platform has plenty of places where string length may get too large.\ndocumentElement.textContent for example. Even though that is not modifying the DOM itself, what should happen on the caller side if there is OOM or otherwise too large string?  (I think Gecko will throw some out-of-memory exception in that case)\n\nInfra talks about something related https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#algorithm-limits",
