    "updated_at": "2025-04-11T10:31:20Z",
    "body": "I think Infra's carveout is less applicable here as `String` has a well-defined length. And `CharacterData` cannot exceed that length. So here we can in fact define reasonable behavior in all the edge cases (such as throwing or not normalizing).",
